<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
                    xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
                    xmlns:b="http://schemas.microsoft.com/xaml/behaviors"
                    xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
                    xmlns:ls="clr-namespace:ls;assembly=Code"
                    xmlns:noesis="clr-namespace:NoesisGUIExtensions;assembly=Noesis.GUI.Extensions"
                    xmlns:System="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib"
                    mc:Ignorable="d">

    <!-- Proficiency at a Glance (PaG): inventory, container and trade cells show whether a character can
         use the item without penalty. Every cell, bag and equipment slot is judged for one character:
         the one picked in the trade window while it is shown, else the selected character.
         The game's slot (Presenter) sits in PaG's cell grid unchanged; over it are the
         marks (shade, glow, badge, dot), and a template trigger can gray it.

         Nothing of PaG's here calls Lua. Lua finds each cell by name (PaGRoot) from inside an
         Ext.UI.Defer callback (Script Extender v33), reads the item's id from the cell's data
         (DataContext.Object.EntityUUID), labels the cell in PaGId on its first write, remembers what
         each cell shows by that label and writes only what changes. Lua is the only writer of a mark.
         On v32 PaG makes no UI calls, so every mark stays hidden and the cell is the game's.

         PaG adds no b:Interaction trigger. A trigger on each cell that passes its owner as the command
         parameter goes with crashes in Interactivity's detach.

         Gray is a template trigger on PaGGray's Opacity, which Lua writes; the template gives the
         Presenter its effect, so Lua never touches the game's markup. Dim is PaGShade, a #66222222
         rectangle (PaG.Brush.Shade) over the art and under the other marks. Lua shows and hides every
         mark through Opacity (1 or 0), never Visibility, so no mark write changes layout. The corner
         switch (PaGSwap, a slot's PaGSlotSwap) is a trigger like gray's: it turns the badge and dot
         half a turn with a RenderTransform, which changes no layout either.

         PaGParts holds every element Lua reads or writes, holds no binding and none of the game's
         markup, and Lua reads only down from it, never up.

         Colors. A brush the XAML created cannot be recolored from Lua: the engine refuses the write,
         without a word for a cell's own brush and with a Noesis "read-only state" error for a shared
         resource. It can be handed around, though: the six palette brushes below are
         shared resources, each cell exposes them through PaGColors (a slot through PaGSlotColors), and
         Lua assigns the brush of the tier's configured color to the badge and the dot. The glow's
         fades are shared the same way, a pair per color (PaG.Glow.*, exposed through PaGGlowColors).
         The glow, badge and dot start with no brush, so they draw nothing until Lua hands them one;
         the shade's brush is fixed.

         Equipment slots (Q13). The helmet, body, gloves, boots and four weapon slots get an overlay
         found the same way (PaGSlotRoot). PaGSlotParts holds the badge and what Lua reads, and Lua
         reads the item's id from the slot's data (DataContext.Item.EntityUUID). Lua judges the item
         for the same one character as the cells and shows the tier's badge icon in the tier color
         for Bad and Not Ideal only; Good gets no mark there.

         The game's keys declared again. A page reaches its panel template, and the template its item
         style and the slot, through StaticResource, resolved inside the game's own files, so a panel
         template keeps the game's slot unless it is declared again too. Below the slot come the item
         styles (the game's two and PaG's), then CharacterInventoryTemplate, PopOutInventoryTemplate,
         ContainerInventoryTemplate, PartyCharacterInventoryTemplate and PartyHolderStyle, copied
         from the game's CharacterSheetTemplates_k.xaml. The first four point their ItemContainerStyle
         at PaG's item styles; PartyHolderStyle is unchanged and is declared again only to reach PaG's
         PartyCharacterInventoryTemplate. At the end, PaG adds its own equipment slot style
         (PaG.EquipmentSlotStyle) and declares the Helmet and CharacterEquipment templates again for
         the same reason. The copies are Larian's, not GPLv3 (NOTICE).
         Better Inventory UI declares all of these keys and BCPP the CharacterSheetTemplates_k ones,
         with the game's content but for BCPP's CharacterEquipmentTemplate (an unused margin and no
         instrument Tag): load this mod after both. -->

    <!-- badge icons: game art used as alpha masks, so a badge takes its tier's color. One per E.Icon
         member, in its order: Good's four, Not Ideal's three, Bad's three (Settings.ICONS), then the
         AC shield, which no tier offers: it stands in for the tier's icon on a mark that only Armor
         vs AC bonuses causes gave (ac_shield_badge) -->
    <ImageBrush x:Key="PaG.Mask.Check" ImageSource="pack://application:,,,/Core;component/Assets/CC/tab_icoCheck_d.png" Stretch="Uniform"/>
    <ImageBrush x:Key="PaG.Mask.CheckThin" ImageSource="pack://application:,,,/Core;component/Assets/Reactions_c/c_ico_reactionOn_active.png" Stretch="Uniform"/>
    <ImageBrush x:Key="PaG.Mask.CheckGlow" ImageSource="pack://application:,,,/Core;component/Assets/Shared_c/c_tick_h.png" Stretch="Uniform"/>
    <ImageBrush x:Key="PaG.Mask.Star" ImageSource="pack://application:,,,/Core;component/Assets/CharacterCreation/ico_proficiency.png" Stretch="Uniform"/>
    <ImageBrush x:Key="PaG.Mask.Warning" ImageSource="pack://application:,,,/Core;component/Assets/Tooltips_c/c_ico_warningSoft.png" Stretch="Uniform"/>
    <ImageBrush x:Key="PaG.Mask.Exclamation" ImageSource="pack://application:,,,/Core;component/Assets/CharacterCreation_c/ico_errorExclamation.png" Stretch="Uniform"/>
    <ImageBrush x:Key="PaG.Mask.Minus" ImageSource="pack://application:,,,/Core;component/Assets/CC/ico_min_d.png" Stretch="Uniform"/>
    <ImageBrush x:Key="PaG.Mask.Cross" ImageSource="pack://application:,,,/Core;component/Assets/CharacterCreation/remover_spellslot.png" Stretch="Uniform"/>
    <ImageBrush x:Key="PaG.Mask.CrossThin" ImageSource="pack://application:,,,/Core;component/Assets/Buttons/ico_btn_cross_d.png" Stretch="Uniform"/>
    <ImageBrush x:Key="PaG.Mask.Skull" ImageSource="pack://application:,,,/Core;component/Assets/Overhead/PassiveRoll/ico_died.png" Stretch="Uniform"/>
    <ImageBrush x:Key="PaG.Mask.Shield" ImageSource="pack://application:,,,/Core;component/Assets/Tooltips/ico_AC.png" Stretch="Uniform"/>
    <!-- the palette: the six colors a tier can take (E.Color), one shared brush each, handed to a
         cell's marks by Lua. Lua cannot recolor them, so these are the colors shown -->
    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="PaG.Brush.Red" Color="#FFE62626"/>
    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="PaG.Brush.Orange" Color="#FFFF991A"/>
    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="PaG.Brush.Yellow" Color="#FFFFD92E"/>
    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="PaG.Brush.Green" Color="#FF33CC4D"/>
    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="PaG.Brush.Blue" Color="#FF3399FF"/>
    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="PaG.Brush.Purple" Color="#FFB35CFF"/>
    <!-- the dim shade (user rule 2): PaGShade's fill, never handed to a mark -->
    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="PaG.Brush.Shade" Color="#66222222"/>
    <!-- the glow's fades (D29), two per palette color in E.Color order: Sides runs across the cell,
         Ends down it. Each is 0.75 alpha (BF) at both edges and clear 12% of the art (9.6 of the
         glow's 76 units: 0.1263) in, then clear to the far 12%. The clear stops keep the color, so the
         fade only loses alpha and never darkens. Offsets are relative, so the fade scales with the
         cell. Lua hands a pair to the glow's two rectangles; it never builds a brush -->
    <LinearGradientBrush x:Key="PaG.Glow.Red.Sides" StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="1,0">
        <GradientStop Color="#BFE62626" Offset="0"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#00E62626" Offset="0.1263"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#00E62626" Offset="0.8737"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#BFE62626" Offset="1"/>
    </LinearGradientBrush>
    <LinearGradientBrush x:Key="PaG.Glow.Red.Ends" StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="0,1">
        <GradientStop Color="#BFE62626" Offset="0"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#00E62626" Offset="0.1263"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#00E62626" Offset="0.8737"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#BFE62626" Offset="1"/>
    </LinearGradientBrush>
    <LinearGradientBrush x:Key="PaG.Glow.Orange.Sides" StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="1,0">
        <GradientStop Color="#BFFF991A" Offset="0"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#00FF991A" Offset="0.1263"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#00FF991A" Offset="0.8737"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#BFFF991A" Offset="1"/>
    </LinearGradientBrush>
    <LinearGradientBrush x:Key="PaG.Glow.Orange.Ends" StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="0,1">
        <GradientStop Color="#BFFF991A" Offset="0"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#00FF991A" Offset="0.1263"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#00FF991A" Offset="0.8737"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#BFFF991A" Offset="1"/>
    </LinearGradientBrush>
    <LinearGradientBrush x:Key="PaG.Glow.Yellow.Sides" StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="1,0">
        <GradientStop Color="#BFFFD92E" Offset="0"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#00FFD92E" Offset="0.1263"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#00FFD92E" Offset="0.8737"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#BFFFD92E" Offset="1"/>
    </LinearGradientBrush>
    <LinearGradientBrush x:Key="PaG.Glow.Yellow.Ends" StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="0,1">
        <GradientStop Color="#BFFFD92E" Offset="0"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#00FFD92E" Offset="0.1263"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#00FFD92E" Offset="0.8737"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#BFFFD92E" Offset="1"/>
    </LinearGradientBrush>
    <LinearGradientBrush x:Key="PaG.Glow.Green.Sides" StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="1,0">
        <GradientStop Color="#BF33CC4D" Offset="0"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#0033CC4D" Offset="0.1263"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#0033CC4D" Offset="0.8737"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#BF33CC4D" Offset="1"/>
    </LinearGradientBrush>
    <LinearGradientBrush x:Key="PaG.Glow.Green.Ends" StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="0,1">
        <GradientStop Color="#BF33CC4D" Offset="0"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#0033CC4D" Offset="0.1263"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#0033CC4D" Offset="0.8737"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#BF33CC4D" Offset="1"/>
    </LinearGradientBrush>
    <LinearGradientBrush x:Key="PaG.Glow.Blue.Sides" StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="1,0">
        <GradientStop Color="#BF3399FF" Offset="0"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#003399FF" Offset="0.1263"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#003399FF" Offset="0.8737"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#BF3399FF" Offset="1"/>
    </LinearGradientBrush>
    <LinearGradientBrush x:Key="PaG.Glow.Blue.Ends" StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="0,1">
        <GradientStop Color="#BF3399FF" Offset="0"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#003399FF" Offset="0.1263"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#003399FF" Offset="0.8737"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#BF3399FF" Offset="1"/>
    </LinearGradientBrush>
    <LinearGradientBrush x:Key="PaG.Glow.Purple.Sides" StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="1,0">
        <GradientStop Color="#BFB35CFF" Offset="0"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#00B35CFF" Offset="0.1263"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#00B35CFF" Offset="0.8737"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#BFB35CFF" Offset="1"/>
    </LinearGradientBrush>
    <LinearGradientBrush x:Key="PaG.Glow.Purple.Ends" StartPoint="0,0" EndPoint="0,1">
        <GradientStop Color="#BFB35CFF" Offset="0"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#00B35CFF" Offset="0.1263"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#00B35CFF" Offset="0.8737"/>
        <GradientStop Color="#BFB35CFF" Offset="1"/>
    </LinearGradientBrush>

    <!-- the game's slot (Presenter, its style and its three triggers) inside PaG's cell grid. The item
         templates and the slot style are StaticResource, as in vanilla: resolved once at load, not per
         cell -->
    <DataTemplate x:Key="Template.InventorySlot" DataType="ls:VMInventorySlot">
        <Grid x:Name="PaGRoot" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center">
            <!-- [1] the art: the game's slot. Style.GameObject sizes the Presenter and the root grid takes
                 that size, so the marks need no size of their own. Lua never reaches it; the gray
                 trigger below gives it its effect. It takes no mouse input: PaG's item styles below
                 drop the game's IsHitTestVisible="False" around the cell so [3] can, and this keeps
                 the art out of hit testing as before -->
            <ContentPresenter x:Name="Presenter" Content="{Binding Object}" Style="{StaticResource Style.GameObject}" IsHitTestVisible="False"/>

            <!-- [2] PaGParts: everything Lua reads or writes. It holds no binding and none of the game's
                 markup, and Lua reads only down from it. Lua reaches each part by child index from
                 here, so the order below is part of the contract (HubConstants.lua C.PART) -->
            <Grid x:Name="PaGParts" IsHitTestVisible="False">
                <!-- [1] dim: a dark shade over the art, under the other marks -->
                <Rectangle x:Name="PaGShade" Fill="{StaticResource PaG.Brush.Shade}" Opacity="0"/>

                <!-- [2] the marks. Nothing here is bound and no brush is set: Lua hands a mark the
                     tier's shared brush, then shows it -->
                <Grid x:Name="PaGMarks">
                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="6*"/>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="80*"/>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="6*"/>
                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                        <RowDefinition Height="6*"/>
                        <RowDefinition Height="80*"/>
                        <RowDefinition Height="6*"/>
                    </Grid.RowDefinitions>

                    <!-- [2.1] inward glow (D29): the tier color fading in from inside the rarity frame. The
                         frame's line is the art's outer 2 of 80 units, so the glow starts 2 in and the
                         line keeps its color. [2.1.1] fades in from the left and right edges, [2.1.2]
                         from the top and bottom, each to nothing 12% of the art deep; the corners get
                         both. Star sizes and relative brushes: it scales with the cell -->
                    <Grid x:Name="PaGGlow" Grid.Column="1" Grid.Row="1" Opacity="0">
                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="2*"/>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="76*"/>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="2*"/>
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                            <RowDefinition Height="2*"/>
                            <RowDefinition Height="76*"/>
                            <RowDefinition Height="2*"/>
                        </Grid.RowDefinitions>
                        <Rectangle x:Name="PaGGlowSides" Grid.Column="1" Grid.Row="1"/>
                        <Rectangle x:Name="PaGGlowEnds" Grid.Column="1" Grid.Row="1"/>
                    </Grid>

                    <!-- [2.2] badge: a dark disc in the top-left corner with the tier's icon in the tier color.
                         [2.2.1.2] to [2.2.1.12] are the icons in E.Icon order, the AC shield last; Lua
                         shows the one the settings name (or the shield) and keeps the others hidden. The corner switch below turns the
                         badge half a turn to the bottom-right and its disc back upright -->
                    <Grid x:Name="PaGBadge" Grid.Column="1" Grid.Row="1" Opacity="0" RenderTransformOrigin="0.5,0.5">
                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="35*" MinWidth="22"/>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="65*"/>
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                            <RowDefinition Height="35*" MinHeight="22"/>
                            <RowDefinition Height="65*"/>
                        </Grid.RowDefinitions>
                        <Grid x:Name="PaGBadgeDisc" RenderTransformOrigin="0.5,0.5">
                            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="15*"/>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="70*"/>
                                <ColumnDefinition Width="15*"/>
                            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                                <RowDefinition Height="15*"/>
                                <RowDefinition Height="70*"/>
                                <RowDefinition Height="15*"/>
                            </Grid.RowDefinitions>
                            <Ellipse Grid.ColumnSpan="3" Grid.RowSpan="3" Fill="#B0000000"/>
                            <Rectangle x:Name="PaGBadgeCheck" Grid.Column="1" Grid.Row="1" OpacityMask="{StaticResource PaG.Mask.Check}" Opacity="0"/>
                            <Rectangle x:Name="PaGBadgeCheckThin" Grid.Column="1" Grid.Row="1" OpacityMask="{StaticResource PaG.Mask.CheckThin}" Opacity="0"/>
                            <Rectangle x:Name="PaGBadgeCheckGlow" Grid.Column="1" Grid.Row="1" OpacityMask="{StaticResource PaG.Mask.CheckGlow}" Opacity="0"/>
                            <Rectangle x:Name="PaGBadgeStar" Grid.Column="1" Grid.Row="1" OpacityMask="{StaticResource PaG.Mask.Star}" Opacity="0"/>
                            <Rectangle x:Name="PaGBadgeWarning" Grid.Column="1" Grid.Row="1" OpacityMask="{StaticResource PaG.Mask.Warning}" Opacity="0"/>
                            <Rectangle x:Name="PaGBadgeExclamation" Grid.Column="1" Grid.Row="1" OpacityMask="{StaticResource PaG.Mask.Exclamation}" Opacity="0"/>
                            <Rectangle x:Name="PaGBadgeMinus" Grid.Column="1" Grid.Row="1" OpacityMask="{StaticResource PaG.Mask.Minus}" Opacity="0"/>
                            <Rectangle x:Name="PaGBadgeCross" Grid.Column="1" Grid.Row="1" OpacityMask="{StaticResource PaG.Mask.Cross}" Opacity="0"/>
                            <Rectangle x:Name="PaGBadgeCrossThin" Grid.Column="1" Grid.Row="1" OpacityMask="{StaticResource PaG.Mask.CrossThin}" Opacity="0"/>
                            <Rectangle x:Name="PaGBadgeSkull" Grid.Column="1" Grid.Row="1" OpacityMask="{StaticResource PaG.Mask.Skull}" Opacity="0"/>
                            <Rectangle x:Name="PaGBadgeShield" Grid.Column="1" Grid.Row="1" OpacityMask="{StaticResource PaG.Mask.Shield}" Opacity="0"/>
                        </Grid>
                    </Grid>

                    <!-- [2.3] dot: a small disc of the tier color in the bottom-right corner (top-left
                         when the corner switch turns it half a turn) -->
                    <Grid x:Name="PaGDot" Grid.Column="1" Grid.Row="1" Opacity="0" RenderTransformOrigin="0.5,0.5">
                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="75*"/>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="25*" MinWidth="12"/>
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                            <RowDefinition Height="75*"/>
                            <RowDefinition Height="25*" MinHeight="12"/>
                        </Grid.RowDefinitions>
                        <Ellipse x:Name="PaGDotShape" Grid.Column="1" Grid.Row="1" Stroke="#E0000000" StrokeThickness="1.5"/>
                    </Grid>
                </Grid>

                <!-- [3] what Lua reads, never shown -->
                <Grid x:Name="PaGIO" Visibility="Collapsed">
                    <!-- [3.1] the label Lua gives the cell on its first write: the key of what Lua knows it shows -->
                    <TextBlock x:Name="PaGId" Text="-"/>
                    <!-- [3.2] the gray switch: Lua writes its Opacity (1 on, 0 off), the template trigger below reads it -->
                    <Grid x:Name="PaGGray" Opacity="0"/>
                    <!-- [3.3] the palette, one holder per color in E.Color order, where Lua can read a
                         brush and hand it to the marks -->
                    <Grid x:Name="PaGColors">
                        <Rectangle x:Name="PaGColorRed" Fill="{StaticResource PaG.Brush.Red}"/>
                        <Rectangle x:Name="PaGColorOrange" Fill="{StaticResource PaG.Brush.Orange}"/>
                        <Rectangle x:Name="PaGColorYellow" Fill="{StaticResource PaG.Brush.Yellow}"/>
                        <Rectangle x:Name="PaGColorGreen" Fill="{StaticResource PaG.Brush.Green}"/>
                        <Rectangle x:Name="PaGColorBlue" Fill="{StaticResource PaG.Brush.Blue}"/>
                        <Rectangle x:Name="PaGColorPurple" Fill="{StaticResource PaG.Brush.Purple}"/>
                    </Grid>
                    <!-- [3.4] the corner switch: Lua writes its Opacity (1 swapped, 0 not), the template
                         trigger below reads it -->
                    <Grid x:Name="PaGSwap" Opacity="0"/>
                    <!-- [3.5] the glow's fades, a Sides and an Ends holder per color in E.Color order,
                         where Lua can read the pair and hand it to the glow -->
                    <Grid x:Name="PaGGlowColors">
                        <Rectangle x:Name="PaGGlowSidesRed" Fill="{StaticResource PaG.Glow.Red.Sides}"/>
                        <Rectangle x:Name="PaGGlowEndsRed" Fill="{StaticResource PaG.Glow.Red.Ends}"/>
                        <Rectangle x:Name="PaGGlowSidesOrange" Fill="{StaticResource PaG.Glow.Orange.Sides}"/>
                        <Rectangle x:Name="PaGGlowEndsOrange" Fill="{StaticResource PaG.Glow.Orange.Ends}"/>
                        <Rectangle x:Name="PaGGlowSidesYellow" Fill="{StaticResource PaG.Glow.Yellow.Sides}"/>
                        <Rectangle x:Name="PaGGlowEndsYellow" Fill="{StaticResource PaG.Glow.Yellow.Ends}"/>
                        <Rectangle x:Name="PaGGlowSidesGreen" Fill="{StaticResource PaG.Glow.Green.Sides}"/>
                        <Rectangle x:Name="PaGGlowEndsGreen" Fill="{StaticResource PaG.Glow.Green.Ends}"/>
                        <Rectangle x:Name="PaGGlowSidesBlue" Fill="{StaticResource PaG.Glow.Blue.Sides}"/>
                        <Rectangle x:Name="PaGGlowEndsBlue" Fill="{StaticResource PaG.Glow.Blue.Ends}"/>
                        <Rectangle x:Name="PaGGlowSidesPurple" Fill="{StaticResource PaG.Glow.Purple.Sides}"/>
                        <Rectangle x:Name="PaGGlowEndsPurple" Fill="{StaticResource PaG.Glow.Purple.Ends}"/>
                    </Grid>
                    <!-- [3.6] Lua writes the badge's and dot's tooltip text (Why.lua), one cause per line;
                         empty: no tooltip (a Good item gets none) -->
                    <TextBlock x:Name="PaGWhy" Text=""/>
                    <!-- [3.7] to [3.14] the same text split for the tooltip's layout (PaGHit): [3.7] its
                         first line, the title, and [3.8] to [3.14] one cause each, "" past the last. Lua
                         writes them before PaGWhy, so a tooltip never shows another item's lines -->
                    <TextBlock x:Name="PaGWhyTitle" Text=""/>
                    <TextBlock x:Name="PaGWhy1" Text=""/>
                    <TextBlock x:Name="PaGWhy2" Text=""/>
                    <TextBlock x:Name="PaGWhy3" Text=""/>
                    <TextBlock x:Name="PaGWhy4" Text=""/>
                    <TextBlock x:Name="PaGWhy5" Text=""/>
                    <TextBlock x:Name="PaGWhy6" Text=""/>
                    <TextBlock x:Name="PaGWhy7" Text=""/>
                </Grid>
            </Grid>

            <!-- [3] PaGHit: the badge's and dot's tooltip. PaGParts takes no mouse input, so a clear target
                 over each mark takes the mouse for it, and PaGHit, their parent, carries the one tooltip
                 both show (a tooltip is found from the element under the mouse up). Lua never reaches it.
                 No background, no mouse of its own; a target takes the mouse only while its mark shows and
                 PaGWhy is not empty (the triggers below), so the rest of the cell keeps the item's
                 tooltip, clicks and drags. Each target is an empty, clear ls:LSEntityObject for the item, bound
                 as the cell root is (DataContext, EntityRef, the root's Context; no context menu of its own)
                 and clipped to a disc that a Viewbox stretches over the mark's corner cell, so a press on a
                 mark lands on the item's element, as elsewhere on the cell (G24). The tooltip shows
                 the mark, the title and one bulleted row per cause (PaGWhyTitle, PaGWhy1 to PaGWhy7). The
                 mark is the badge, or the dot while only the dot shows: PaGBadgeHit takes the mouse
                 exactly while the badge shows with a text. Same geometry as PaGMarks; the corner switch
                 turns it with the marks. -->
            <Grid x:Name="PaGHit" ToolTipService.ShowOnDisabled="True">
                <Grid.ToolTip>
                    <ls:LSTooltip>
                        <StackPanel>
                            <!-- the mark, then the title ("Not Ideal for Shadowheart") -->
                            <DockPanel Margin="0,0,0,12">
                                <Grid DockPanel.Dock="Left" Width="48" Height="48" Margin="0,0,16,0" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                    <!-- the badge, or the dot while only the dot shows: the badge's target takes the mouse
                                         exactly while the badge shows with a text -->
                                    <Grid Visibility="{Binding IsHitTestVisible, ElementName=PaGBadgeHit, Converter={StaticResource BoolToVisibleConverter}}">
                                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                            <ColumnDefinition Width="15*"/>
                                            <ColumnDefinition Width="70*"/>
                                            <ColumnDefinition Width="15*"/>
                                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                                            <RowDefinition Height="15*"/>
                                            <RowDefinition Height="70*"/>
                                            <RowDefinition Height="15*"/>
                                        </Grid.RowDefinitions>
                                        <Ellipse Grid.ColumnSpan="3" Grid.RowSpan="3" Fill="#B0000000"/>
                                        <Rectangle Grid.Column="1" Grid.Row="1" OpacityMask="{StaticResource PaG.Mask.Check}" Fill="{Binding Fill, ElementName=PaGBadgeCheck}" Opacity="{Binding Opacity, ElementName=PaGBadgeCheck}"/>
                                        <Rectangle Grid.Column="1" Grid.Row="1" OpacityMask="{StaticResource PaG.Mask.CheckThin}" Fill="{Binding Fill, ElementName=PaGBadgeCheckThin}" Opacity="{Binding Opacity, ElementName=PaGBadgeCheckThin}"/>
                                        <Rectangle Grid.Column="1" Grid.Row="1" OpacityMask="{StaticResource PaG.Mask.CheckGlow}" Fill="{Binding Fill, ElementName=PaGBadgeCheckGlow}" Opacity="{Binding Opacity, ElementName=PaGBadgeCheckGlow}"/>
                                        <Rectangle Grid.Column="1" Grid.Row="1" OpacityMask="{StaticResource PaG.Mask.Star}" Fill="{Binding Fill, ElementName=PaGBadgeStar}" Opacity="{Binding Opacity, ElementName=PaGBadgeStar}"/>
                                        <Rectangle Grid.Column="1" Grid.Row="1" OpacityMask="{StaticResource PaG.Mask.Warning}" Fill="{Binding Fill, ElementName=PaGBadgeWarning}" Opacity="{Binding Opacity, ElementName=PaGBadgeWarning}"/>
                                        <Rectangle Grid.Column="1" Grid.Row="1" OpacityMask="{StaticResource PaG.Mask.Exclamation}" Fill="{Binding Fill, ElementName=PaGBadgeExclamation}" Opacity="{Binding Opacity, ElementName=PaGBadgeExclamation}"/>
